Z||000000||Haze_Performance||03-29-2000||06:46 AM||||I have looked at tons of fiero sites, most of them sell the same type of body mods. Im looking for a complete hood (not a stock one)ram air look or something cool. Im looking for some cool body mods without turning the car into a kit. Anyone have any rare pic's of Fiero parts that are just bolt on???.....Thanks for your help...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||phillip||03-29-2000||08:05 AM|||| i got that big fiero parts book. pretty much any thing you can get for a fiero is in there. they just updated it but i don't have the new one.<P> along the same line i'm wondering what people have have adapted from other cars to their fieros. if some one works in or knows someone who works in a aftermarket custom shop, how about holding some of the custom ground effects, especialy those big front spoilers and/or chin guards up to the fiero to see how hard it would be to glass one in? i keep thinking something from a mustang ('80's and up ) or a 3000gt 0r stealth might work, because they're both fairly wide for small cars. i know mustangs are really close as i have a mustang wing on mine now.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||03-29-2000||10:27 AM||||Just got the latest edition of the Big Fiero Parts Book. Has LOTS of stuff. <BR>I have also been looking for some unique body mods (scoops and stuff). Thinking about getting a bunch of catalogs from "Year One". They sell 60s & 70s musclecar parts. Thought I might find some small bolt-on scoops that would adapt "tastefully" to a Fiero.<BR>FOCOA used to have a replacement hood that had a rather large "reverse flow" opening in it. (I'll call it a GT40 look, but that probably isn't too accurate.)  Looks really nice but is very expensive.||||reg||1
